From 677dd6f452ec67a6ef3eb69651affd1b630c9f61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Micha=C5=82=20=C5=BBygowski?= <michal.zygowski@3mdeb.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:20:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] feat(tpm): add an EL3 firmware TPM based on ms-tpm-20-ref

Proof of concept firmware TPM running in BL31: the Microsoft TPM 2.0
reference implementation (ms-tpm-20-ref v1.83, TpmBigNum on wolfCrypt),
built as libftpm with its own TpmConfiguration overrides and a minimal libc
glue (heap, time, entropy from FEAT_RNG or a timer seeded PRNG). Commands run
on a dedicated 256KB stack.

The OS interface is a TCG CRB with the Arm SMC start method
(ftpm_crb_start()). The ftpm_drtm_reset_pcrs() and ftpm_drtm_extend() give the
D-CRTM locality 4 access to PCR 17-22.

Not secure: the TPM NV state is volatile (manufactured on every cold boot)
and the CRB is in NS memory.

Signed-off-by: Michał Żygowski <michal.zygowski@3mdeb.com>
